# React 19

Applies alongside `docs/ENGINEERING.md` (this repo: **PascalCase** `.tsx` component filenames, **kebab-case** for non-component modules, **`features/`** layout).

## TypeScript

- TypeScript for components, hooks, and utilities.
- **`interface`** for props and object-shaped models.
- Typed state: **`useState<T>()`**; avoid **`any`** — use `unknown` + narrowing when needed.

## Files and exports

- Colocate by feature under **`src/features/<domain>/`** (see engineering doc).
- **`.tsx`** for JSX; **`.ts`** for hooks and utils without JSX.
- **Default export** for route `page.tsx` / `layout.tsx` and full-page modules when Next requires it; otherwise prefer **named exports** for reusable pieces so refactors and tree-shaking stay predictable. Hooks and utilities: **named exports**.

## Naming

- Components: **PascalCase** (`UserProfile`).
- Hooks: **`use` + PascalCase** (`useUserData`).
- Server Actions / mutation helpers: clear verbs (`updateUserProfile`).
- **Filenames:** match `docs/ENGINEERING.md` — component files **PascalCase**; other TS modules **kebab-case**.

## Imports

- Group: **React** → **third-party** → **`@/…` local**.
- Prefer **`@/`**; avoid relative imports deeper than **two** levels.

## Purity

- Same props/state → same JSX; **no side effects during render** (no subscriptions, timers, or uncached `fetch` in render).
- **Do not mutate** props or state; treat updates as replacements.
- For async data in Client Components, use a **stable** `Promise` with **`use`** (e.g. passed from a parent or cache), **Server Components** for initial load, or **`useEffect`** when the flow is genuinely client-only — not a fresh `Promise` constructed inline every render.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD: new Promise every render breaks `use`
function Bad() {
  const data = use(fetch("/api")); // unstable
  return null;
}

// ✅ GOOD: stable promise from props/cache
function Good({ userPromise }: { userPromise: Promise<User> }) {
  const user = use(userPromise);
  return <span>{user.name}</span>;
}
```

## Rules of Hooks

- Only call hooks at the **top level** of components or custom hooks — not inside loops, conditions, or nested callbacks.
- **Exhaustive-deps:** keep `useEffect` / `useMemo` / `useCallback` dependency arrays honest (or eslint-disable with a comment only when justified).

## Memoization and React Compiler

- If **React Compiler** is enabled for this project, prefer **clear, small components** and let the compiler memoize; avoid **`useMemo` / `useCallback` / `memo`** unless **profiling** shows a hotspot.
- If the compiler is **not** enabled, apply manual memoization sparingly and only where measured.

## Components

- **Function components only** — no class components.
- **Composition** over inheritance; use **`children`** and small building blocks; compound components when they improve readability.
- Prefer **small files** (roughly under **100 lines** of component logic) so boundaries stay testable.

## Refs (React 19)

- **`ref` as a normal prop** on function components is supported — avoid **`forwardRef`** for new code unless you must support older React types.
- **Ref callbacks** may return a **cleanup** function (runs on unmount or before re-run).

```tsx
function Panel({ ref }: { ref?: React.Ref<HTMLDivElement | null> }) {
  return <div ref={ref}>…</div>;
}
```

## Document metadata (client trees)

- You may render **`<title>`**, **`<meta>`**, **`<link>`** in component output where appropriate; React hoists them. Prefer **Next `metadata` / `generateMetadata`** for App Router pages when possible.

## `useState`

- Prefer **functional updates** when the next value depends on the previous: `setN((x) => x + 1)`.
- **Lift state** only to the nearest shared parent.

## `use` (React 19)

- Read **Promises** and **Context** during render; the tree must be under **`<Suspense>`** for thrown promises.
- Do not pass a **new** Promise each render (see purity example).

## `useEffect`

- Sync with external systems (subscriptions, DOM, timers); **return cleanup** when needed.
- Do not use `useEffect` as the default data-loading strategy in App Router — prefer **Server Components** or **server-backed** patterns from `nextjs-app-router` rule.

## `useDeferredValue`

- Defer expensive child updates; React 19 supports an **`initialValue`** option for the first deferred render when applicable.

## `useOptimistic`

- Pair with **Server Actions** or other mutations for responsive UI; keep the reducer **pure**.

## Context

- React 19 allows rendering **`<MyContext value={v}>`** as a provider shorthand (same as **`MyContext.Provider`**). Keep context **narrow** (theme, small UI flags), not a full app data store.

## Custom hooks

- Prefix **`use`**; call other hooks only at top level; return stable object shapes when consumers depend on referential equality (especially without compiler).

## Forms and Actions

- Server mutations: **`"use server"`** actions (see Next rule). Client form state: **`useActionState`** from **`react`**.

```tsx
"use client";

import { useActionState } from "react";

export function Form({ action }: { action: (prev: State, formData: FormData) => Promise<State> }) {
  const [state, formAction, pending] = useActionState(action, null);
  return (
    <form action={formAction}>
      <button type="submit" disabled={pending}>
        Save
      </button>
      {state?.error ? <p>{state.error}</p> : null}
    </form>
  );
}
```

- **`useFormStatus`** for submit pending state inside **form descendants** — import from **`react-dom`**.

```tsx
"use client";

import { useFormStatus } from "react-dom";

export function SubmitButton({ label }: { label: string }) {
  const { pending } = useFormStatus();
  return (
    <button type="submit" disabled={pending}>
      {label}
    </button>
  );
}
```

## Concurrent usage

- Wrap non-urgent state updates in **`startTransition`** to keep input responsive.
- Use **`<Suspense>`** for async children, lazy chunks, and `use`-driven loading.

## Anti-patterns

**Avoid:** mutating props/state; conditional hooks; **`any`**; `useEffect` as default data layer in RSC apps; **`forwardRef`** in new code unless required; blanket **`memo` / `useCallback`** without evidence.

**Prefer:** explicit types; pure render; Server Components + Actions where appropriate; **`use`** with stable promises; small components; compiler-aware memoization policy.
